# Test-driven development

## Iron law

```
NO PRODUCTION CODE WITHOUT A FAILING TEST FIRST
```

1. **RED** — write failing test for intended behavior
2. **Verify failure** — wrong/missing behavior, not typos
3. **GREEN** — minimal production code to pass
4. **Refactor** — only after green; keep tests passing

## Coverage by layer

| Layer | Tool | Focus |
|-------|------|-------|
| Pure logic | Vitest / pytest | merchant normalization, subscription detection, insight scoring, env validation |
| Contracts | Vitest | Zod schema round-trip, request/response shapes |
| API routes | Vitest + mocks | Zod validation, auth + ownership, status codes, queue/storage side effects, rate limits |
| Workers | Vitest + mocks | job contracts, retries, idempotency, low-confidence path |
| AI service | pytest + mocks | OpenAI Structured Outputs, fixture extraction tolerance, PII guard, internal token |
| UI | Vitest + Testing Library | components, loading/empty/error states, optimistic mutations |
| E2E | Playwright | sign in → upload fixture → see extracted receipt + insight (Phase 9) |

## Commands

```bash
pnpm run test                    # all JS/TS workspaces (web, worker, lib, ui, contracts)
cd services/ai && pytest tests -q
pnpm --filter @receiptbrain/web test:e2e   # when present
```

## AI fixtures

Fixture-driven tests live in `fixtures/receipts/`: each `.jpg|.png|.pdf` has a matching `.json` ground truth. AI extract tests assert merchant exact, total within ±$0.01, item count exact.

If test tooling is missing, scaffold it in Phase 0 before feature work.

## Completion rule

Never claim "done" or "passing" without command output showing green tests for the changed area.

## Exceptions (explicit approval only)

Docs-only, pure config, generated code.
